cks potential. They fail because early investors accumulate too much of the supply, then dump their bags and drain the liquidity, leaving everyone else holding the bag.\n\nBut what if we could change that?\n\nWith Liquidy, we’re introducing a new standard for token launches: a system that turns trading fees into liquidity that is burned, buybacks, and long-term ecosystem growth.\n\n💧 HOW LIQUIFY WORKS\n\n100% of the creator fees generated by $LIQUIFY are put to work:\n\n• 50% buys back $LIQUIFY.\n• 50% stays in SOL.\nBoth assets are added to the liquidity pool and the LP is burned. Liquidity never leaves.\n\n🚀 LAUNCH YOUR OWN TOKEN ON LIQUIFY\n\nAnyone can launch a token on pumpfun through Liquify. Every token is paired with $LIQUIFY, so every buy from SOL routes through $LIQUIFY first. The fee structure is designed to benefit the token, not to generate revenue for the protocol.\n\nFor every token launched on Liquify, after bonding:\n\n• 45% of fees buys back the launched token.\n• 45% stays in $LIQUIFY.\n• 10% of fees is burned in $LIQUIFY.\n\nBoth sides are added to the token’s PumpSwap liquidity pool and the LP is burned. Nothing waits in a wallet: every claim is deposited within a minute.\n🌊 WHAT IF YOUR TOKEN HASN’T BONDED YET?\nLiquidity doesn’t have to wait for bonding.\n\nBefore bonding, every fee your token generates is a buyback and burn:\n\n• 90% buys back and burns your token.\n• 10% is burned in $LIQUIFY.\n\nOnce your token bonds, the mechanism shifts to building its PumpSwap liquidity pool.\n\nEvery trade contributes. Every fee has a purpose. Every action is a public transaction you can verify on the Engine page.","icon":"lEGYEkFUbZnAhjAk","header":"https://cdn.dexscreener.com/cms/images/WlvhJWfRjHjg9ACz?width=900&height=300&fit=crop&quality=95&format=auto","openGraph":"https://cdn.dexscreener.com/token-images/og/solana/AEqqTu9iYMvzWJa8Ub9XtQaN1awYw3uyUEPJxVe9pump?timestamp=1792146300000","links":[{"url":"https://liquify.trade/"},{"type":"twitter","url